# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/ship-4 window (the combined ship candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/ship-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-ship-4/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# TC1 (STOP): the AUDITED CONCURRENT TIER arm (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-concurrent, scenario tier_concurrent) on the candidate's audited twin
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-audit: a session built to the largest size the profile admits, fresh-salt floods the size of the KV pool (16,500
# blocks here, not the 19,968 the tier pack ran on) so that it leaves the device pool for host RAM, SEVEN SEATS decoding (about 4k-token coding prompts, ignore_eos), a 10 s
# settle and a 60 s CONTROL window of the seats alone, then the session RETURNS (restored from host RAM; it decodes 512 tokens as an eighth seat), a long (120k) fresh
# prompt (SPILL) and the returning turn's COLD TWIN (a fresh salt, the same body; strict pair). THE NEW THING HERE: the seven seats and the returning eighth run on the OCTO
# block (QWEN_FAST_OCTO_MIN_LIVE=6), so the tier's restore and spill happen inside a scheduler step while octo rounds are the steady state. READ (the tier pack's TC1,
# references/fusion-jobs/tier): the plan verdict PASS, every pair IDENTICAL, a "host tier restore" line for the returning turn at the oracle's Q, "host tier spill" lines
# inside the long prompt's request, the failure counters (spill, restore, digest, read-back mismatch) ZERO, no pins held, every one of the seven seats decoding across the
# control, restore, restore_decode and spill windows (else NOT_EXERCISED), and the lines "window <name>: ... round time p50/p99/mean ..., longest wait ... s". Also:
# "[OCTO]" round lines with shape=octo during the control window (the seats ARE on the octo block) and none of the octo judge's hard problems (python3
# scripts/ci/octo_judge.py --container-log <container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-audit; its eight-live lever rules do not apply at
# seven seats: read what it reports about shape and admission). The stall is PRINTED here, not judged (the audits are this arm's cost); the budget is judged on TC2 to TC5.
# Unqualified: a measurement, never evidence. Duration (estimate): 90 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-concurrent
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
